119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Before taking CREA 7100 at BCIT, I thought ethics in design was a fairly small idea, such as not plagiarizing or just being a decent human being. I had not yet captured the full picture.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Now I see a much bigger and more personal scope. It is about who I want to be when a client pressures me, or when I am on a tight deadline and tempted to cut corners.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The frameworks we studied helped me most. Virtue ethics in particular, which is the idea that good decisions come from building good character over time rather than just following a list of rules, changed how I think about my own practice. It is not about what you are allowed to do. It is about who you are becoming.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (I am still figuring out where I stand on AI and authorship. But I think being confused and honest is better than being somehow certain and wrong.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
